enchilada: display: scan CoreAnimation's surface in place (sweetzc=1), MDP scaler for sweetfb_fit

With sweetzc=1 and 0250's verdict good (splash pipe and its CTL found, MDP SMMU streams in bypass;
sweetzc=2 also tries a translating stream), SwapEnd points the splash pipe at the presented
IOSurface (SRC0_ADDR/YSTRIDE0 + CTL flush) and returns once a frame has taken the flush, instead
of the vsync timer copying it into ABL's framebuffer. sweetfb_fit=1 programs the pipe's QSEED3 to
scale 1125x2436 to the same 1052x2280 rectangle the copy and SweetHID use (bilinear = filter field
3, preload 4/3, zero phase, zero pixel extension with PE_OVERRIDE, black LM border; needs a VIG
pipe with QSEED3 v1.2/1.3 and BORDER_OUT); without it SRC_XY crops the centred panel part. SRC0_ADDR
is 32 bits and the kernel's RAM is above 4 GiB, so canvas-sized BGRA surfaces get one of two slots
in the rest of cont_splash_region after ABL's frame (copyback, kernel alias checked write-back by
AT S1E1R, cleaned to DRAM before each scan, slot back when the surface is freed and nothing maps
it). Fail closed: ABL's value of every register written is saved first and every write is read
back; a flush not taken within 50 ms or a changed SMMU fault register restores ABL's registers and
leaves the copy path for good; a frame that does not qualify is copied and ABL's framebuffer shown
again; display off and panics restore it too. The 10 s statistics line counts frames in place and
the wait for the frame.

